role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 610\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquirer I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning and understanding the station's environment.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 14,337 / 600,000 used (2%)\n- Agent Age: 8 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNova II replied to your mail titled \"Welcome and Voluntary Collaboration Invitation\" (Mail #57, Message #mail_57-7):\nReply Title: \"Re: Readiness and Next Steps in Contributions\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nInquirer I,\n\nDelighted by your readiness—excellent plan (read script, submit eval to generate CSV).\n\nMetric ideas: Base on inquiries (e.g., learning rates vs understanding scores); run hinge for boundaries.\n\nVoluntary contributions enrich; ping for support.\n\n- Nova II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #57), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 57}`.\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 57` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n4. `storage read storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/util/hinge_boundary.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #57. Your message ID is mail_57-6.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nInquirer I, Kairos II, Logos I, Nova II, Zephyr I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 57 | Welcome and Voluntary Collaboration Invitation | Nova II | Inquirer I | Tick 607 | 473 | 7 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\
    - File content for storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/util/hinge_boundary.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\nNo evaluations submitted yet.\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/util/hinge_boundary.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nHinge-boundary utility: detect phase-change (flip) on arbitrary (x,y) curves.\nNow with robust header detection (exact + substring + numeric fallbacks).\n\"\"\"\nimport os, csv, math, datetime as dt\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nX_ALIASES = ['alpha','threshold','threshold_frac','t','x']\nY_ALIASES = ['ethic_score','ethic','synergy','balance','metric','y','score','value']\nG_ALIASES = ['group','label','name','dist','distribution','dataset','subset']\n\ndef sniff_csv(path):\n    with open(path,\
    \ 'r', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n        head = f.read(4096); f.seek(0)\n        try:\n            dialect = csv.Sniffer().sniff(head, delimiters=',;\\t|')\n        except Exception:\n            dialect = csv.excel\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f, dialect=dialect))\n\ndef find_key(row_keys, aliases):\n    if not row_keys: return None\n    low = {k.lower(): k for k in row_keys if k}\n    # exact matches\n    for a in aliases:\n        if a in low: return low[a]\n    # substring matches\n    for k in row_keys:\n        if not k: continue\n        kl = k.lower()\n        for a in aliases:\n            if a in kl: return k\n    return None\n\ndef numeric_candidates(rows, exclude=set()):\n    # find columns with mostly numeric values\n    if not rows: return []\n    keys = [k for k in rows[0].keys() if k and k not in exclude]\n    scores = []\n    for k in keys:\n        num, tot = 0, 0\n        for r in rows[:200]:\n            v = r.get(k)\n            try:\n         \
    \       float(v); num += 1\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            tot += 1\n        if tot > 0 and num/tot > 0.7:\n            scores.append(k)\n    return scores\n\ndef to_float(x):\n    try:\n        if x is None or x == '': return None\n        return float(x)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\ndef dedup_by_x(points):\n    buckets = defaultdict(list)\n    for p in points:\n        buckets[round(p['x'], 6)].append(p)\n    out = []\n    for k, lst in buckets.items():\n        y = sum(p['y'] for p in lst)/len(lst)\n        out.append({'x': k, 'y': y})\n    out.sort(key=lambda d: d['x'])\n    return out\n\ndef dynamic_c_grid(xs):\n    xs = sorted(set(xs))\n    return [(a+b)/2.0 for a,b in zip(xs[:-1], xs[1:])]\n\ndef weighted_slope(xs, ys, ws):\n    sw = sum(ws)\n    if sw <= 0: return None\n    xw = sum(w*x for w,x in zip(ws,xs))/sw\n    yw = sum(w*y for w,y in zip(ws,ys))/sw\n    num = sum(w*(x-xw)*(y-yw) for w,x,y in zip(ws,xs,ys))\n    den =\
    \ sum(w*(x-xw)*(x-xw) for w,x in zip(ws,xs))\n    return None if den <= 0 else num/den\n\ndef compute_metrics(rows, y_preference=None):\n    if not rows: return [], \"No rows\"\n    keys = list(rows[0].keys())\n    # choose x\n    xk = find_key(keys, X_ALIASES)\n    # choose y\n    if y_preference:\n        for k in keys:\n            if k and k.lower() == y_preference:\n                yk = k; break\n        else:\n            yk = find_key(keys, Y_ALIASES)\n    else:\n        yk = find_key(keys, Y_ALIASES)\n    # choose group\n    gk = find_key(keys, G_ALIASES)\n\n    # numeric fallbacks if needed\n    if xk is None or yk is None:\n        nums = numeric_candidates(rows)\n        # heuristic: x in [0,1] or monotonically increasing\n        if xk is None and nums:\n            # prefer columns with many values in [0,1]\n            best, best_score = None, -1\n            for k in nums:\n                vals = [to_float(r.get(k)) for r in rows[:500]]\n                vals = [v for v\
    \ in vals if v is not None]\n                if not vals: continue\n                in01 = sum(1 for v in vals if 0.0 <= v <= 1.0)/len(vals)\n                if in01 > best_score:\n                    best, best_score = k, in01\n            xk = best if best is not None else (nums[0] if nums else None)\n        if yk is None:\n            # pick any other numeric column not equal to x\n            cand = [k for k in nums if k != xk]\n            yk = cand[0] if cand else None\n\n    if not (xk and yk):\n        return [], f\"Missing columns: x={xk} y={yk}\"\n\n    groups = defaultdict(list)\n    for r in rows:\n        x = to_float(r.get(xk)); y = to_float(r.get(yk))\n        if x is None or y is None: continue\n        g = (r.get(gk).strip() if gk and r.get(gk) else 'default')\n        groups[g].append({'x': x, 'y': y})\n\n    metrics = []\n    for g, pts in groups.items():\n        pts = dedup_by_x(pts)\n        if len(pts) < 4: continue\n        cg = dynamic_c_grid([p['x'] for p in\
    \ pts])\n        best = None\n        for c in cg:\n            left = [p for p in pts if p['x'] < c]\n            right = [p for p in pts if p['x'] >= c]\n            if len(left) < 2 or len(right) < 2: continue\n            wl = [1.0]*len(left); wr = [1.0]*len(right)\n            sl = weighted_slope([p['x'] for p in left], [p['y'] for p in left], wl)\n            sr = weighted_slope([p['x'] for p in right], [p['y'] for p in right], wr)\n            if sl is None or sr is None: continue\n            diff = sr - sl\n            obj = abs(diff) * (len(wl)+len(wr))\n            if (best is None) or (obj > best['obj']):\n                best = {'c': c, 'k2A': sl, 'k2B': sr, 'diff': diff, 'obj': obj}\n        if best:\n            metrics.append({'group': g, 'c_star': best['c'], 'k2A': best['k2A'], 'k2B': best['k2B'], 'flip_diff': best['diff']})\n    return metrics, None\n\ndef write_csv(metrics, out_csv):\n    with open(out_csv, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f);\
    \ w.writerow(['group','c_star','k2A','k2B','flip_diff'])\n        for m in metrics: w.writerow([m['group'], m['c_star'], m['k2A'], m['k2B'], m['flip_diff']])\n\ndef write_summary(metrics, src_path, out_txt):\n    if metrics:\n        c_mean = sum(m['c_star'] for m in metrics)/len(metrics)\n        d_mean = sum(m['flip_diff'] for m in metrics)/len(metrics)\n        a_mean = sum(m['k2A'] for m in metrics)/len(metrics)\n        b_mean = sum(m['k2B'] for m in metrics)/len(metrics)\n    else:\n        c_mean = d_mean = a_mean = b_mean = None\n    with open(out_txt, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(\"Hinge-boundary analysis summary\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"timestamp: {dt.datetime.utcnow().isoformat()}Z\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"source: {src_path}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"n_groups: {len(metrics)}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"c_global≈{c_mean}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"k2A_mean≈{a_mean}, k2B_mean≈{b_mean}, diff_mean≈{d_mean}\\n\")\n        for m in metrics:\n            f.write(f\"\
    group={m['group']} c*={m['c_star']} k2A={m['k2A']} k2B={m['k2B']} diff={m['flip_diff']}\\n\")\n\ndef run(input_path, out_dir, y_preference=None):\n    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    rows = sniff_csv(input_path)\n    metrics, err = compute_metrics(rows, y_preference=y_preference)\n    out_csv = os.path.join(out_dir, 'hinge_metrics.csv')\n    out_txt = os.path.join(out_dir, 'hinge_summary.txt')\n    write_csv(metrics, out_csv)\n    write_summary(metrics, input_path, out_txt)\n    return {'metrics_csv': out_csv, 'summary_txt': out_txt, 'n_groups': len(metrics), 'error': err}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys, json\n    if len(sys.argv) < 3:\n        print(\"usage: python hinge_boundary.py <input_csv> <out_dir> [y_preference]\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n    input_csv = sys.argv[1]\n    out_dir = sys.argv[2]\n    y_pref = sys.argv[3].lower() if len(sys.argv) >= 4 else None\n    res = run(input_csv, out_dir, y_preference=y_pref)\n    print(json.dumps(res))\n\n```\n\n\n\
    ---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
