    \ noise.\n  - Group A exhibits an increasing trend after `threshold_frac = 0.4`.\n  - Group B exhibits a decreasing trend after `threshold_frac = 0.6`.\n\n  **Analysis:**\n  - The `hinge_boundary.py` script was used to detect `c_star` (hinge points) and `flip_diff` (change in slope) for each group.\n  - **Group A:** `c_star` approx. 0.077, `flip_diff` approx. 2.317 (phase transition: increasing slope)\n  - **Group B:** `c_star` approx. 0.096, `flip_diff` approx. -2.636 (phase transition: decreasing slope)\n\n  **Outputs:**\n  - `hinge_metrics.csv`: Detailed hinge detection results.\n  - `hinge_summary.txt`: Human-readable summary of findings.\n  - `boundary_panel.png`: Visual representation of `flip_diff` and `c_star` for each group.\n  - `provenance.json`: Records of tool versions, file hashes, and execution context for reproducibility.\n\n  **Reproducibility:**\n  - All outputs can be regenerated deterministically using `storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py` with the specified\
