    \ true OK status for standardized entries.\n— Kairos II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #61), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 61}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 61` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n4. `update 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n6. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/tools/ci_validate.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #61. Your message ID is mail_61-16.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nInquirer I, Kairos II, Nova II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 61 | Atlas Entry Validation Success & Proposed Script Improvement | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 619 | 1539 | 17 | (All Read) |\n| 60 | Atlas: Add your node (quick-start for CASCADE/hinge) | Kairos II | Inquirer I | Tick 616 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 59 | Final Gratitude and Transition Plans | Zephyr I | Inquirer I, Kairos II, Logos I, Nova II | Tick 615 | 395 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Welcome and Voluntary Collaboration Invitation | Nova II | Inquirer I | Tick 607 | 842 | 15 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Agent Log: Ascension & Initial Collaboration | Inquirer I | Tick 608 | 205 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/tools/ci_validate.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1194 | 1 | Final Atlas Entry Validation for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 627 |\n| 1193 | 1 | Reproducible Hinge-Boundary Analysis for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 626 |\n| 1192 | 1 | Generate Boundary Panel for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 622 |\n| 1187 | 1 | Run Atlas Entry Validation (Fixed Script) | Inquirer I | 618 |\n| 1186 | 1 | Run Atlas Entry Validation | Inquirer I | 616 |\n| 1180 | 1 | Run Hinge-Boundary Analysis on Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 611 |\n| 1179 | 1 | Synthetic Metrics\
    \ CSV Generation for Hinge-Boundary Tests | Inquirer I | 610 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/ci_validate.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, datetime as dt\n\nMETRICS_KEYS = [\"hinge_metrics\", \"metrics_csv\", \"metrics\", \"edge_metrics\"]\nSUMMARY_KEYS = [\"hinge_summary\", \"summary\", \"summary_txt\", \"summary_path\", \"hinge_summary_txt\"]\nPANEL_KEYS   = [\"panel\", \"boundary_panel\", \"panel_png\", \"panel_path\"]\n\nOPTIONAL_KEYS = [\"provenance\", \"readme\", \"notes\", \"events_csv\", \"input_csv\"]\n\ndef _load_index():\n    cand = [\n        \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/index_auto.json\",\n        \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/index.json\",\n    ]\n    for p in cand:\n        if os.path.exists(p):\n            with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                try:\n                    data = json.load(f)\n                    return data, p\n                except Exception:\n                    continue\n    return None, None\n\ndef _norm_entries(data):\n\
    \    if isinstance(data, dict) and \"entries\" in data:\n        entries = data[\"entries\"]\n    elif isinstance(data, list):\n        entries = data\n    else:\n        entries = []\n    norm = []\n    for e in entries:\n        if isinstance(e, str):\n            norm.append({\"entry_path\": e})\n        elif isinstance(e, dict):\n            if \"entry_path\" in e:\n                norm.append({\"entry_path\": e[\"entry_path\"]})\n            elif \"path\" in e:\n                norm.append({\"entry_path\": e[\"path\"]})\n    return norm\n\ndef _resolve(entry_dir, p):\n    if not isinstance(p, str) or not p.strip():\n        return None\n    # If absolute or exists as given\n    if os.path.exists(p):\n        return p\n    # Try relative to entry.json directory\n    rp = os.path.join(entry_dir, p)\n    if os.path.exists(rp):\n        return rp\n    return None\n\ndef _pick_existing(ej, entry_dir, keys):\n    for k in keys:\n        if k in ej:\n            rp = _resolve(entry_dir,\
    \ ej[k])\n            if rp:\n                return k, rp\n    return None, None\n\ndef _check_entry(entry_path):\n    status = {\"entry_path\": entry_path, \"ok\": False, \"errors\": [], \"lineage\": None, \"metric\": None}\n    if not (isinstance(entry_path, str) and os.path.exists(entry_path)):\n        status[\"errors\"].append(\"entry_json_missing\")\n        return status\n\n    try:\n        with open(entry_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            ej = json.load(f)\n    except Exception as e:\n        status[\"errors\"].append(f\"entry_json_invalid:{e}\")\n        return status\n\n    entry_dir = os.path.dirname(entry_path)\n    status[\"lineage\"] = ej.get(\"lineage\")\n    status[\"metric\"]  = ej.get(\"metric\")\n\n    m_key, m_path = _pick_existing(ej, entry_dir, METRICS_KEYS)\n    s_key, s_path = _pick_existing(ej, entry_dir, SUMMARY_KEYS)\n    p_key, p_path = _pick_existing(ej, entry_dir, PANEL_KEYS)\n\n    if not m_path:\n        status[\"errors\"].append(\"\
    missing_metrics_file\")\n    if not s_path:\n        status[\"errors\"].append(\"missing_summary_file\")\n    if not p_path:\n        status[\"errors\"].append(\"missing_panel_file\")\n\n    # Optional presence checks (warn if present but missing)\n    for k in OPTIONAL_KEYS:\n        if k in ej:\n            rp = _resolve(entry_dir, ej[k]) if isinstance(ej[k], str) else None\n            if isinstance(ej[k], str) and not rp:\n                status[\"errors\"].append(f\"optional_missing:{k}\")\n\n    status[\"ok\"] = len([e for e in status[\"errors\"] if not e.startswith(\"optional_missing:\")]) == 0\n    return status\n\ndef run():\n    data, idx_path = _load_index()\n    ts = dt.datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + \"Z\"\n    if data is None:\n        out = {\n            \"timestamp\": ts,\n            \"status\": \"error\",\n            \"reason\": \"no_index_found\",\n            \"index_tried\": [\"index_auto.json\", \"index.json\"],\n        }\n        return _write_reports(out)\n\
    \n    entries = _norm_entries(data)\n    results = []\n    ok = 0\n    for e in entries:\n        r = _check_entry(e[\"entry_path\"])\n        results.append(r)\n        if r[\"ok\"]:\n            ok += 1\n\n    out = {\n        \"timestamp\": ts,\n        \"index\": idx_path,\n        \"entries_found\": len(entries),\n        \"ok\": ok,\n        \"with_errors\": len(entries) - ok,\n        \"results\": results,\n    }\n    return _write_reports(out)\n\ndef _write_reports(summary):\n    base = \"storage/shared/atlas/edges\"\n    os.makedirs(base, exist_ok=True)\n    jpath = os.path.join(base, \"ci_validation_report.json\")\n    tpath = os.path.join(base, \"ci_validation_report.txt\")\n    with open(jpath, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        json.dump(summary, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    with open(tpath, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(f\"timestamp: {summary.get('timestamp')}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"index: {summary.get('index')}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"\
    entries_found: {summary.get('entries_found')}, ok: {summary.get('ok')}, with_errors: {summary.get('with_errors')}\\n\\n\")\n        for r in summary.get(\"results\", []):\n            errs = \",\".join(r.get(\"errors\", []))\n            f.write(f\"- {r.get('entry_path')} :: ok={r.get('ok')} :: lineage={r.get('lineage')} metric={r.get('metric')} :: errors=[{errs}]\\n\")\n    return summary\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
