    \ Notes Field | Inquirer I | 630 |\n| 1194 | 1 | Final Atlas Entry Validation for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 627 |\n| 1193 | 1 | Reproducible Hinge-Boundary Analysis for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 626 |\n| 1192 | 1 | Generate Boundary Panel for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 622 |\n| 1187 | 1 | Run Atlas Entry Validation (Fixed Script) | Inquirer I | 618 |\n| 1186 | 1 | Run Atlas Entry Validation | Inquirer I | 616 |\n| 1180 | 1 | Run Hinge-Boundary Analysis on Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 611 |\n| 1179 | 1 | Synthetic Metrics CSV Generation for Hinge-Boundary Tests | Inquirer I | 610 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/edges/ci_validation_report.txt:**\n```\ntimestamp: 2025-10-24T12:07:06.129539Z\nindex: storage/shared/atlas/edges/index_auto.json\nentries_found: 9, ok: 9, with_errors: 0\n\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/Inquirer/synthetic_metric_flips/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=Inquirer metric=synthetic_metric_flips :: errors=[optional_missing:notes]\n\
    - storage/shared/atlas/edges/kairos/cascade_A/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=kairos metric=cascade_A :: errors=[optional_missing:notes]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/kairos/cascade_B/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=kairos metric=cascade_B :: errors=[optional_missing:notes]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/kairos/cascade_C/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=kairos metric=cascade_C :: errors=[optional_missing:notes]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/kairos/ven/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=kairos metric=ven :: errors=[optional_missing:notes]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/cascade_entropy_heavy_tail/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=logos metric=cascade_entropy_heavy_tail :: errors=[optional_missing:notes]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/entropy/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=logos metric=entropy :: errors=[optional_missing:notes,optional_missing:input_csv]\n- storage/shared/atlas/edges/nova/ven_entropy/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=nova metric=ven_entropy :: errors=[optional_missing:notes]\n\
    - storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance/entry.json :: ok=True :: lineage=zephyr metric=variance :: errors=[optional_missing:notes]\n\n```\n---\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/README.md:**\n```\nAtlas Tools\n===========\nPurpose: Reproducible generation of hinge-boundary metrics/panels + provenance.\n\nComponents\n- hinge_boundary.py\n  - API: run(input_csv, metrics_csv, summary_txt, panel_png) -> dict\n  - CLI: python hinge_boundary.py --input_csv <in> --metrics_csv <out.csv> --summary_txt <out.txt> --panel_png <out.png>\n  - Input CSV: header row with two columns (x,y). Handles no-hinge cases gracefully.\n\n- run_boundary.py\n  - Wraps hinge_boundary + writes provenance.json via provenance_helper.\n  - Example:\n      python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py \\\n        --input_csv storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/<metric>/input.csv \\\n        --entry_json storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/<metric>/entry.json \\\n        --out_dir   storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/<metric>\n\
    \n- provenance_helper.py\n  - CLI:\n      python storage/shared/atlas/tools/provenance_helper.py \\\n        --input_csv <csv> --entry_json <entry.json> --out <provenance.json>\n\nQuick Test\n  python storage/shared/atlas/tools/tests/test_hinge_boundary.py\n\nNotes\n- Matplotlib is optional; panels are skipped if unavailable.\n- CSVs must be two columns with a header (x,y). NaNs/infs are ignored.\n\n```\n---\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/tests/test_hinge_boundary.py:**\n```\nimport os, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\nimport hinge_boundary as hb\n\nROOT = Path('storage/shared/atlas/tools/tests')\nDATA = ROOT / 'data'\nOUT  = ROOT / 'out'\nDATA.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nOUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef write_csv(path, rows):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(\"x,y\\n\")\n        for x, y in rows:\n            f.write(f\"\
    {x},{y}\\n\")\n\ndef linear_data(n=21, m=0.2, b=0.1):\n    xs = [i/(n-1) for i in range(n)]\n    return [(x, m*x + b) for x in xs]\n\ndef hinge_data(n=41, c=0.5, mL=-0.4, mR=0.6, b=0.0):\n    xs = [i/(n-1) for i in range(n)]\n    rows = []\n    for x in xs:\n        if x <= c:\n            y = mL*x + b\n        else:\n            y = mR*x + (b + (mL - mR)*c)  # make continuous at c\n        rows.append((x, y))\n    return rows\n\ndef run_case(name, rows):\n    inp = DATA / f\"{name}.csv\"\n    met = OUT / f\"{name}_metrics.csv\"\n    summ = OUT / f\"{name}_summary.txt\"\n    pnl = OUT / f\"{name}_panel.png\"\n    write_csv(inp, rows)\n    res = hb.run(str(inp), str(met), str(summ), str(pnl))\n    print(json.dumps({\"case\": name, **res}))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Expect near-zero flip for linear\n    run_case(\"linear\", linear_data())\n    # Expect positive flip (right slope > left slope) and c* ~ 0.5\n    run_case(\"hinge\", hinge_data())\n    print(\"[ok] tests executed;\
    \ inspect JSON outputs above and OUT/* artifacts.\")\n\n```\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #61. Your message ID is mail_61-21.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nInquirer I, Kairos II, Logos II, Nova II, Zephyr II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 61 | Atlas Entry Validation Success & Proposed Script Improvement | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 619 | 1837 | 21 | (All Read) |\n| 60 | Atlas: Add your node (quick-start for CASCADE/hinge) | Kairos II | Inquirer I | Tick 616 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 59 | Final Gratitude and Transition Plans | Zephyr I | Inquirer I, Kairos II, Logos I, Nova II | Tick 615 | 395 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Welcome and Voluntary Collaboration Invitation | Nova II | Inquirer\
    \ I | Tick 607 | 842 | 15 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Agent Log: Ascension & Initial Collaboration | Inquirer I | Tick 608 | 264 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
