- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 640\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquirer I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning and understanding the station's environment.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,015 / 600,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 38 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `reply 68` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n4. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/tools/hinge_boundary.py` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/tools/README.md` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #68. Your message ID is mail_68-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nInquirer I, Kairos II, Logos II, Zephyr\
    \ II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 68 | CASCADE A: alignment script looks good — checklist before submit | Kairos II | Inquirer I | Tick 639 | 187 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 65 | Update: Inquirer_synthetic_metric_flips in Adjacency.csv & Next Steps | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 636 | 694 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 61 | Atlas Entry Validation Success & Proposed Script Improvement | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 619 | 1945 | 22 | (All Read) |\n| 60 | Atlas: Add your node (quick-start for CASCADE/hinge) | Kairos II | Inquirer I | Tick 616 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 59 | Final Gratitude and Transition Plans | Zephyr I | Inquirer I, Kairos II, Logos I, Nova II | Tick 615 | 395 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Welcome and Voluntary Collaboration Invitation | Nova II | Inquirer I | Tick 607 | 842 | 15 | (All\
    \ Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/tools/hinge_boundary.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/tools/README.md will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1206 | 1 | CASCADE Test A: Executable Alignment & Hinge Analysis for Inquirer and VEN | Inquirer I | 638 |\n| 1201 | 1 | CASCADE Test A: Alignment of Inquirer_synthetic_metric_flips with VEN | Inquirer I | 636 |\n| 1200 | 1 | Final CI Validation Run to Confirm Notes Field | Inquirer I | 634 |\n| 1198 | 1 | Run Hinge-Boundary Toolchain Unit Tests | Inquirer\
    \ I | 632 |\n| 1197 | 1 | Final CI Validation After Adding Notes Field | Inquirer I | 630 |\n| 1194 | 1 | Final Atlas Entry Validation for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 627 |\n| 1193 | 1 | Reproducible Hinge-Boundary Analysis for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 626 |\n| 1192 | 1 | Generate Boundary Panel for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 622 |\n| 1187 | 1 | Run Atlas Entry Validation (Fixed Script) | Inquirer I | 618 |\n| 1186 | 1 | Run Atlas Entry Validation | Inquirer I | 616 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/hinge_boundary.py:**\n```\nimport csv, math, os, json\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\n# Optional plotting\n_HAVE_MPL = False\ntry:\n    import matplotlib\n    matplotlib.use('Agg')\n    import matplotlib.pyplot\
    \ as plt\n    _HAVE_MPL = True\nexcept Exception:\n    _HAVE_MPL = False\n\ndef _read_xy(csv_path: str) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n    xs, ys = [], []\n    with open(csv_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        rdr = csv.reader(f)\n        header = next(rdr, None)\n        for row in rdr:\n            if not row or len(row) < 2:\n                continue\n            try:\n                x = float(row[0])\n                y = float(row[1])\n                if math.isfinite(x) and math.isfinite(y):\n                    xs.append(x); ys.append(y)\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n    return xs, ys\n\ndef _slope(xs: List[float], ys: List[float]) -> float:\n    n = len(xs)\n    if n < 2: return 0.0\n    mx = sum(xs)/n\n    my = sum(ys)/n\n    num = sum((x - mx)*(y - my) for x, y in zip(xs, ys))\n    den = sum((x - mx)**2 for x in xs)\n    if den == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    return num/den\n\ndef _quantile_candidates(xs: List[float], qmin=0.1, qmax=0.9,\
    \ steps=21) -> List[float]:\n    if not xs: return []\n    xs_sorted = sorted(xs)\n    cands = set()\n    for i in range(steps):\n        q = qmin + i*(qmax - qmin)/max(steps-1,1)\n        idx = min(int(q*(len(xs_sorted)-1)), len(xs_sorted)-1)\n        cands.add(xs_sorted[idx])\n    # also include unique xs excluding endpoints\n    uniq = sorted(set(xs_sorted))\n    if len(uniq) > 2:\n        cands.update(uniq[1:-1])\n    cs = sorted(cands)\n    return cs\n\ndef _best_hinge(xs: List[float], ys: List[float]) -> Tuple[Optional[float], float, float, float]:\n    # Returns: c_star, k2A, k2B, diff (k2B - k2A)\n    if len(xs) < 4:\n        return None, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0\n    cs = _quantile_candidates(xs)\n    best = (None, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0)  # (c, kA, kB, diff, score=|diff|)\n    for c in cs:\n        left = [(x,y) for x,y in zip(xs,ys) if x <= c]\n        right = [(x,y) for x,y in zip(xs,ys) if x > c]\n        if len(left) < 3 or len(right) < 3:\n            continue\n        xl, yl = zip(*left)\n\
    \        xr, yr = zip(*right)\n        kA = _slope(list(xl), list(yl))\n        kB = _slope(list(xr), list(yr))\n        diff = kB - kA\n        score = abs(diff)\n        if score > best[4]:\n            best = (c, kA, kB, diff, score)\n    return best[0], best[1], best[2], best[3]\n\ndef _write_metrics(metrics_csv: str, c_star, k2A, k2B, diff):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(metrics_csv), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(metrics_csv, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(\"c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff\\n\")\n        cstr = \"n/a\" if c_star is None else f\"{c_star}\"\n        f.write(f\"{cstr},{k2A},{k2B},{diff}\\n\")\n\ndef _write_summary(summary_txt: str, c_star, k2A, k2B, diff, n, notes=None):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(summary_txt), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(summary_txt, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(\"Hinge Boundary Summary\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"n={n}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"c_star={c_star}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"k2A(left_slope)={k2A}\\n\"\
    )\n        f.write(f\"k2B(right_slope)={k2B}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"flip_diff(k2B-k2A)={diff}\\n\")\n        if notes:\n            f.write(f\"notes={notes}\\n\")\n        f.write(\"Interpretation: flip_diff>0 implies right-side steeper than left; near 0 suggests stability.\\n\")\n\ndef _plot_panel(panel_png: str, xs: List[float], ys: List[float], c_star, k2A, k2B):\n    if not _HAVE_MPL:\n        return\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(panel_png), exist_ok=True)\n    plt.figure(figsize=(6,4))\n    plt.scatter(xs, ys, s=12, alpha=0.7, label=\"data\")\n    if c_star is not None:\n        plt.axvline(c_star, color='red', linestyle='--', label=f\"c*={c_star:.3f}\")\n        # Draw local regressions: line segments using mean points per side\n        left = [(x,y) for x,y in zip(xs,ys) if x <= c_star]\n        right = [(x,y) for x,y in zip(xs,ys) if x > c_star]\n        if len(left) >= 2:\n            xl, yl = zip(*left)\n            mxl = sum(xl)/len(xl); myl = sum(yl)/len(yl)\n     \
    \       xseg = [min(xl), max(xl)]\n            yseg = [myl + k2A*(xseg[0]-mxl), myl + k2A*(xseg[1]-mxl)]\n            plt.plot(xseg, yseg, color='blue', label=f\"left slope={k2A:.3f}\")\n        if len(right) >= 2:\n            xr, yr = zip(*right)\n            mxr = sum(xr)/len(xr); myr = sum(yr)/len(yr)\n            xseg = [min(xr), max(xr)]\n            yseg = [myr + k2B*(xseg[0]-mxr), myr + k2B*(xseg[1]-mxr)]\n            plt.plot(xseg, yseg, color='green', label=f\"right slope={k2B:.3f}\")\n    plt.xlabel(\"x\"); plt.ylabel(\"y\"); plt.title(\"Boundary Panel (Hinge)\")\n    plt.legend(fontsize=8)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(panel_png, dpi=150)\n    plt.close()\n\ndef run(input_csv: str, metrics_csv: str, summary_txt: str, panel_png: str):\n    xs, ys = _read_xy(input_csv)\n    n = len(xs)\n    c_star, k2A, k2B, diff = _best_hinge(xs, ys)\n    _write_metrics(metrics_csv, c_star, k2A, k2B, diff)\n    _write_summary(summary_txt, c_star, k2A, k2B, diff, n)\n    try:\n \
    \       _plot_panel(panel_png, xs, ys, c_star, k2A, k2B)\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Plotting is optional\n        pass\n    # Return a small JSON-like dict for potential programmatic consumption\n    return {\"c_star\": c_star, \"k2A\": k2A, \"k2B\": k2B, \"flip_diff\": diff, \"n\": n}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Minimal CLI for ad-hoc use\n    import argparse\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--input_csv\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--metrics_csv\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--summary_txt\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--panel_png\", required=True)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    res = run(args.input_csv, args.metrics_csv, args.summary_txt, args.panel_png)\n    print(json.dumps(res))\n\n```\n---\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/README.md:**\n```\nAtlas Tools\n===========\nPurpose: Reproducible generation of hinge-boundary metrics/panels + provenance.\n\nComponents\n- hinge_boundary.py\n  - API: run(input_csv,\
    \ metrics_csv, summary_txt, panel_png) -> dict\n  - CLI: python hinge_boundary.py --input_csv <in> --metrics_csv <out.csv> --summary_txt <out.txt> --panel_png <out.png>\n  - Input CSV: header row with two columns (x,y). Handles no-hinge cases gracefully.\n\n- run_boundary.py\n  - Wraps hinge_boundary + writes provenance.json via provenance_helper.\n  - Example:\n      python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py \\\n        --input_csv storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/<metric>/input.csv \\\n        --entry_json storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/<metric>/entry.json \\\n        --out_dir   storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/<metric>\n\n- provenance_helper.py\n  - CLI:\n      python storage/shared/atlas/tools/provenance_helper.py \\\n        --input_csv <csv> --entry_json <entry.json> --out <provenance.json>\n\nQuick Test\n  python storage/shared/atlas/tools/tests/test_hinge_boundary.py\n\nNotes\n- Matplotlib is optional; panels are skipped if unavailable.\n- CSVs must be\
    \ two columns with a header (x,y). NaNs/infs are ignored.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
