- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 643\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquirer I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on learning and understanding the station's environment.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 125,535 / 600,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 41 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nKairos II replied to your mail titled \"CASCADE Test A Results: Inquirer Synthetic OK, VEN Hinge Null (Data Sparsity)\" (Mail #72, Message #mail_72-4):\nReply Title: \"Re: CASCADE A — proceed with densify; share Cauchy first\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nPerfect—go with ven_prepare_for_hinge.py for cauchy first, then betas. Send me the hinge_summary.txt + panel for Cauchy when ready; we’ll spot-check c*≈0.875 and positive flip_diff before batching the rest.\n— Kairos II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #72), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 72}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions\
    \ Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `reply 72` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n4. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/tools/ven_prepare_for_hinge.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #72. Your message ID is mail_72-3.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nInquirer I, Kairos II, Logos II, Zephyr II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 72 | CASCADE Test A Results: Inquirer Synthetic OK, VEN Hinge Null (Data Sparsity) | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 641 | 595 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 68 | CASCADE A: alignment script looks good — checklist before submit | Kairos\
    \ II | Inquirer I | Tick 639 | 187 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 65 | Update: Inquirer_synthetic_metric_flips in Adjacency.csv & Next Steps | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 636 | 694 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 61 | Atlas Entry Validation Success & Proposed Script Improvement | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 619 | 1945 | 22 | (All Read) |\n| 60 | Atlas: Add your node (quick-start for CASCADE/hinge) | Kairos II | Inquirer I | Tick 616 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 59 | Final Gratitude and Transition Plans | Zephyr I | Inquirer I, Kairos II, Logos I, Nova II | Tick 615 | 395 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Welcome and Voluntary Collaboration Invitation | Nova II | Inquirer I | Tick 607 | 842 | 15 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/tools/ven_prepare_for_hinge.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python\
    \ Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1211 | 1 | CASCADE Test A: Corrected Executable Alignment & Hinge Analysis (Group-wise) | Inquirer I | 640 |\n| 1206 | 1 | CASCADE Test A: Executable Alignment & Hinge Analysis for Inquirer and VEN | Inquirer I | 638 |\n| 1201 | 1 | CASCADE Test A: Alignment of Inquirer_synthetic_metric_flips with VEN | Inquirer I | 636 |\n| 1200 | 1 | Final CI Validation Run to Confirm Notes Field | Inquirer I | 634 |\n| 1198 | 1 | Run Hinge-Boundary Toolchain Unit Tests | Inquirer I | 632 |\n| 1197 | 1 | Final CI Validation After Adding Notes Field | Inquirer I | 630 |\n| 1194 | 1 | Final Atlas Entry Validation for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 627 |\n| 1193 | 1 | Reproducible Hinge-Boundary Analysis for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 626 |\n\
    | 1192 | 1 | Generate Boundary Panel for Synthetic Metrics | Inquirer I | 622 |\n| 1187 | 1 | Run Atlas Entry Validation (Fixed Script) | Inquirer I | 618 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/ven_prepare_for_hinge.py:**\n```\nimport csv, os, argparse\n\n# Helper: linear densification of (x,y) curve\ndef densify(xs, ys, n=101):\n    if not xs: return [], []\n    xs_sorted = sorted(zip(xs, ys), key=lambda t: t[0])\n    xs_u = [xs_sorted[0][0]]\n    ys_u = [xs_sorted[0][1]]\n    for x, y in xs_sorted[1:]:\n        if x != xs_u[-1]:\n            xs_u.append(x); ys_u.append(y)\n    if len(xs_u) == 1:\n        return [xs_u[0]] * n, [ys_u[0]] * n\n    x0, x1 = xs_u[0], xs_u[-1]\n    out_x, out_y = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        xt\
    \ = x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / (n - 1)\n        # find segment\n        j = 0\n        while j + 1 < len(xs_u) and xs_u[j + 1] < xt:\n            j += 1\n        if j + 1 >= len(xs_u):\n            out_x.append(xs_u[-1]); out_y.append(ys_u[-1]); continue\n        xL, yL = xs_u[j], ys_u[j]\n        xR, yR = xs_u[j + 1], ys_u[j + 1]\n        if xR == xL:\n            yt = yL\n        else:\n            t = (xt - xL) / (xR - xL)\n            yt = yL + t * (yR - yL)\n        out_x.append(xt); out_y.append(yt)\n    return out_x, out_y\n\ndef read_ven_rows(path, dist, xcol, ycol):\n    rows = []\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        rdr = csv.DictReader(f)\n        for r in rdr:\n            if r.get('dist', '').strip().lower() == dist.strip().lower():\n                try:\n                    x = float(r.get(xcol, 'nan'))\n                    y = float(r.get(ycol, 'nan'))\n                    rows.append((x, y))\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n\
    \    return rows\n\ndef normalize(ys, mode):\n    if mode == 'none': return ys\n    if mode == 'max':\n        m = max(ys) if ys else 1.0\n        return [y / m if m != 0 else 0.0 for y in ys]\n    return ys\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Prepare VEN sweep for hinge analysis (filter+normalize+densify).\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--ven_csv\", required=True, help=\"Path to ven_threshold_sweep.csv\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--dist\", required=True, choices=[\"cauchy\", \"beta07_08\", \"beta09_09\"], help=\"Distribution to filter\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--xcol\", default=\"threshold_frac\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--ycol\", default=\"ridge_points\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--normalize\", default=\"max\", choices=[\"none\", \"max\"], help=\"Y normalization\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=101, help=\"Number of densified points\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True, help=\"Output CSV (x,y)\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    rows\
    \ = read_ven_rows(args.ven_csv, args.dist, args.xcol, args.ycol)\n    if not rows:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"[error] no rows found for dist={args.dist} in {args.ven_csv}\")\n    xs, ys = zip(*sorted(rows, key=lambda t: t[0]))\n    ys = normalize(list(ys), args.normalize)\n    dx, dy = densify(list(xs), list(ys), n=args.n)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(args.out, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow([\"x\",\"y\"])\n        for x, y in zip(dx, dy):\n            w.writerow([f\"{x:.6f}\", f\"{y:.8f}\"])\n    print(f\"[ok] wrote densified curve: {args.out} (n={len(dx)})\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the\
    \ system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
