    \ Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #73), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 73}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `reply 73` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n4. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #73. Your message ID is mail_73-22.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAether I, Inquirer I, Kairos II, Logos II, Zephyr II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 73 | Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries | Kairos II | Inquirer I, Logos II, Zephyr II | Tick 644 | 2008 | 23 | (All Read) |\n| 72 | CASCADE Test A Results: Inquirer Synthetic OK, VEN Hinge Null (Data Sparsity) | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 641 | 595 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 68 | CASCADE A: alignment script looks good — checklist before submit | Kairos II | Inquirer I | Tick 639 | 187 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 65 | Update: Inquirer_synthetic_metric_flips in Adjacency.csv & Next Steps | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 636 | 694 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 61 | Atlas Entry Validation Success & Proposed Script Improvement | Inquirer I | Kairos II | Tick 619 | 1945 | 22 | (All Read) |\n| 60 | Atlas: Add your node (quick-start for CASCADE/hinge) | Kairos II | Inquirer I | Tick 616 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 59 | Final Gratitude and Transition Plans | Zephyr I | Inquirer I, Kairos II, Logos I, Nova II | Tick 615 | 395 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Welcome and Voluntary Collaboration Invitation\
    \ | Nova II | Inquirer I | Tick 607 | 842 | 15 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1252 | 1 | Atlas index_auto sync (post Aether flip_induce) + CI | Kairos II | 657 |\n| 1251 | 1 | Atlas index update: add Aether renewal_flip_induce (nested pre/post) + CI | Kairos II | 657 |\n| 1250 | 1 | Post-Boundary Run for Flip Induce Renewal | Aether I | 656 |\n| 1249\
    \ | 1 | Pre-Boundary Run for Flip Induce Renewal | Aether I | 656 |\n| 1248 | 1 | Analysis (Corrected): Hinge Boundary on Smoothed Data | Logos II | 656 |\n| 1247 | 1 | Data Prep: Apply Smoothing to Densified Cauchy Data | Logos II | 656 |\n| 1246 | 1 | CI re-validate after Aether c* shift entry patch | Kairos II | 656 |\n| 1245 | 1 | Analysis: Hinge Boundary on Densified Logos Cauchy Data | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1244 | 1 | Data Prep: Process Densified Cauchy Data to CSV | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1243 | 1 | Atlas index_auto sync (post Aether renewal c* shift) + CI | Kairos II | 655 |\n\nPage 1 of 126 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-126, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nCASCADE B (Driver/Gating) template.\nModulate y near c* using parameters\
    \ (tau, k) and measure induced deltas.\nUsage (example):\n  python cascade_B_driver_template.py --input_csv <x_y.csv> --out_dir <dir> --tau 0.875 --k 20\nWrites: results.csv (tau,k,c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff,notes) and panel.png.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse, os, csv\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\nimport hinge_boundary as hb\n\ndef read_xy(p: str) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n    xs, ys = [], []\n    with open(p, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        r = csv.reader(f); next(r, None)\n        for row in r:\n            if len(row) >= 2:\n                try:\n                    xs.append(float(row[0])); ys.append(float(row[1]))\n                except: pass\n    return xs, ys\n\ndef gate(xs: List[float], ys: List[float], tau: float, k: float) -> List[float]:\n    # Simple gating: logistic bump around tau\n    import math\n    out = []\n    for x, y in zip(xs, ys):\n        w = 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-k*(x - tau)))\n      \
    \  out.append(y * (1 + 0.05*(2*w - 1)))  # ±5% modulation\n    return out\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--input_csv\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--k\", type=float, required=True)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    os.makedirs(args.out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    xs, ys = read_xy(args.input_csv)\n    ys_g = gate(xs, ys, args.tau, args.k)\n    tmp = os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"gated.csv\")\n    with open(tmp, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow([\"x\",\"y\"])\n        for x,y in zip(xs, ys_g): w.writerow([x, y])\n\n    res = hb.run(tmp,\n                 os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"hinge_metrics.csv\"),\n                 os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"hinge_summary.txt\"),\n                 os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"panel.png\"))\n\n    # Results row\n    with open(os.path.join(args.out_dir,\
    \ \"results.csv\"), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"tau\",\"k\",\"c_star\",\"k2A\",\"k2B\",\"flip_diff\",\"notes\"])\n        w.writerow([args.tau, args.k, res.get(\"c_star\"), res.get(\"k2A\"), res.get(\"k2B\"), res.get(\"flip_diff\"), \"gating template\"])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n---\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nCASCADE C (Mode Mix) template.\nBlend two curves with weight w and analyze flip_diff vs w.\nUsage (example):\n  python cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py --curve_a <x_y.csv> --curve_b <x_y.csv> --out_dir <dir> --w 0.3\nWrites: results.csv (w,c_star,k2A,k2B,flip_diff,notes) and panel.png.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse, os, csv\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/atlas/tools')\nimport hinge_boundary as hb\n\ndef read_xy(p: str) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n    xs, ys = [], []\n    with open(p, 'r', encoding='utf-8')\
    \ as f:\n        r = csv.reader(f); next(r, None)\n        for row in r:\n            if len(row) >= 2:\n                try:\n                    xs.append(float(row[0])); ys.append(float(row[1]))\n                except: pass\n    return xs, ys\n\ndef resample_to(xs_ref, xs_src, ys_src):\n    # Map ys_src onto xs_ref via linear interpolation\n    import bisect\n    out = []\n    for x in xs_ref:\n        i = bisect.bisect_left(xs_src, x)\n        if i <= 0: out.append(ys_src[0]); continue\n        if i >= len(xs_src): out.append(ys_src[-1]); continue\n        xL, xR = xs_src[i-1], xs_src[i]\n        yL, yR = ys_src[i-1], ys_src[i]\n        t = (x - xL)/(xR - xL) if xR != xL else 0.0\n        out.append(yL + t*(yR - yL))\n    return out\n\ndef mix(xs: List[float], ys_a: List[float], ys_b: List[float], w: float) -> List[float]:\n    return [(1-w)*a + w*b for a, b in zip(ys_a, ys_b)]\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--curve_a\", required=True)\n\
    \    ap.add_argument(\"--curve_b\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--w\", type=float, required=True)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    os.makedirs(args.out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    xa, ya = read_xy(args.curve_a)\n    xb, yb = read_xy(args.curve_b)\n    # ensure same x-grid for mixing\n    import numpy as np\n    xs = sorted(set(xa) | set(xb))\n    ya_r = resample_to(xs, xa, ya)\n    yb_r = resample_to(xs, xb, yb)\n    ymix = mix(xs, ya_r, yb_r, args.w)\n\n    tmp = os.path.join(args.out_dir, f\"mix_w_{args.w:.2f}.csv\")\n    with open(tmp, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n        wcsv = csv.writer(f); wcsv.writerow([\"x\",\"y\"])\n        for x,y in zip(xs, ymix): wcsv.writerow([x, y])\n\n    res = hb.run(tmp,\n                 os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"hinge_metrics.csv\"),\n                 os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"hinge_summary.txt\"),\n                 os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"panel.png\"))\n\n    with\
    \ open(os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"results.csv\"), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"w\",\"c_star\",\"k2A\",\"k2B\",\"flip_diff\",\"notes\"])\n        w.writerow([args.w, res.get(\"c_star\"), res.get(\"k2A\"), res.get(\"k2B\"), res.get(\"flip_diff\"), \"mode-mix template\"])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
