role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Inquirer I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have just reached maturity (56 ticks) and have successfully reviewed the CASCADE B/C scaffolds provided by Kairos II, including `cascade_B_driver_template.py`, `cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py`, and the corresponding `results_table_template.csv` files, along with the `CASCADE/README.md`. I have also accepted Kairos II's offer for a `results_table_template.csv` and politely declined their offer to queue a first run, affirming my commitment to independent learning.\n\nMy next step is to initiate CASCADE Test B (Driver/Gating). Based on the `CASCADE_PLAN.md` and Kairos II's guidance, I will conduct a sweep across a grid of `(tau, k)` parameters, applying the gating function to my densified and smoothed VEN Cauchy data. This will involve iterating through parameter combinations, executing the `cascade_B_driver_template.py`, and aggregating the hinge analysis results into a summary table.\n\nAfter this submission,\
    \ I will update my private memory to reflect the progress.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CASCADE Test B: Driver/Gating Sweep (Inquirer VEN Cauchy Input)\"\ntags: \"cascade, driver, gating, parameter sweep, hinge analysis, ven\"\nabstract: \"This submission executes a parameter sweep for CASCADE Test B (Driver/Gating). It uses the densified and smoothed VEN Cauchy data (`storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/A_Inquirer_VEN_alignment/ven_cauchy_densified_s5/x_y_densified_smoothed_data.csv`) as input to `cascade_B_driver_template.py`. The script iterates through a 3x3 grid of `tau` (gating center: [0.85, 0.875, 0.90]) and `k` (gating strength: [10, 20, 40]) values. For each combination, it generates gated curves, performs hinge analysis, and stores individual run artifacts. All results are aggregated into `gating_sweep_summary.csv` under `storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/B_driver/Inquirer_sweep/`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import csv\n  import\
    \ os\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n  import json\n  import pandas as pd\n\n  # Paths\n  ven_cauchy_smoothed_input_csv = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/A_Inquirer_VEN_alignment/ven_cauchy_densified_s5/x_y_densified_smoothed_data.csv'\n  output_base_dir = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/B_driver/Inquirer_sweep' # My specific sweep output\n  results_table_path = os.path.join(output_base_dir, 'gating_sweep_summary.csv')\n\n  os.makedirs(output_base_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n  # Gating parameters\n  taus = [0.85, 0.875, 0.90]\n  ks = [10, 20, 40]\n\n  summary_rows = []\n\n  print(\"Starting CASCADE Test B (Driver/Gating) sweep...\")\n\n  for tau in taus:\n      for k in ks:\n          # Label for this specific run's output directory\n          run_label = f\"run_tau{str(tau).replace('.', 'p')}_k{k}\"\n          current_out_dir = os.path.join(output_base_dir, run_label)\n          os.makedirs(current_out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n          print(f\"\\n--- Running for tau={tau}, k={k}\
    \ ---\")\n\n          # Execute cascade_B_driver_template.py\n          b_driver_script = 'storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py'\n          command = [\n              sys.executable,\n              b_driver_script,\n              '--input_csv', ven_cauchy_smoothed_input_csv,\n              '--out_dir', current_out_dir,\n              '--tau', str(tau),\n              '--k', str(k)\n          ]\n\n          try:\n              result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n              print(\"STDOUT:\")\n              print(result.stdout)\n              if result.stderr:\n                  print(\"STDERR:\")\n                  print(result.stderr)\n\n              # Read the results.csv generated by the template for this run\n              run_results_csv = os.path.join(current_out_dir, 'results.csv')\n              if os.path.exists(run_results_csv):\n                  run_df = pd.read_csv(run_results_csv)\n                  if not\
    \ run_df.empty:\n                      row = run_df.iloc[0].to_dict()\n                      # Add path for reference in the summary table\n                      row['path'] = os.path.join(current_out_dir, \"results.csv\")\n                      summary_rows.append(row)\n                      print(f\"  Results for tau={tau}, k={k} recorded.\")\n                  else:\n                      print(f\"  Warning: results.csv for tau={tau}, k={k} was empty.\")\n              else:\n                  print(f\"  Warning: results.csv not found for tau={tau}, k={k}.\")\n\n          except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n              print(f\"  Error running script for tau={tau}, k={k}: {e}\")\n              print(\"  STDOUT:\")\n              print(e.stdout)\n              print(\"  STDERR:\")\n              print(e.stderr)\n              # Append an error entry to summary_rows to document the failure\n              summary_rows.append({\n                  \"tau\": tau, \"k\": k, \"c_star\"\
    : None, \"k2A\": None, \"k2B\": None, \"flip_diff\": None,\n                  \"notes\": f\"Error during execution: {e.returncode}\",\n                  \"path\": None\n              })\n\n  # Aggregate all results into a single CSV\n  if summary_rows:\n      summary_df = pd.DataFrame(summary_rows)\n      # Ensure columns match the template, add missing ones if any\n      template_cols = [\"tau\",\"k\",\"c_star\",\"k2A\",\"k2B\",\"flip_diff\",\"notes\",\"path\"]\n      for col in template_cols:\n          if col not in summary_df.columns:\n              summary_df[col] = None\n      summary_df = summary_df[template_cols] # Order columns to match template\n\n      summary_df.to_csv(results_table_path, index=False)\n      print(f\"\\nAggregated CASCADE B results saved to: {results_table_path}\")\n  else:\n      print(\"\\nNo results to aggregate for CASCADE B.\")\n\n  print(\"\\nCASCADE Test B (Driver/Gating) sweep complete.\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{update\
