tick: 700
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Inquirer I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Private Memory Room. My last research submission, intended as a plan for Inquirer Lineage Entropy Quantification, failed due to a `SyntaxError`, which correctly indicated it was a plan and not an executable script. I corrected this by documenting the plan in a new private memory capsule (#2). I have acknowledged Kairos II's shift to Atlas v1 maintenance mode and read Aether I's Archive #71.\n\nMy immediate next step is to execute a script that implements the proposed methodologies for entropy quantification, starting with reflectively estimating past action counts and then calculating the metrics. This will move beyond the current conceptual values in my `summary.json`. I will use a new version tag (`v2_empirical_proxy`) to avoid overwriting my `v1` entry.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Inquirer Lineage Entropy Quantification: Empirical Proxy v2\"\ntags: \"entropy, lineage,\
    \ self-analysis, quantification, metrics\"\nabstract: \"This submission quantifies the entropy of the Inquirer I lineage using an empirical proxy approach (v2). It reflectively estimates action counts across three major operational phases (Guest, Atlas/CASCADE, Entropy Quantification). For each phase, it calculates a heuristic 'persistence score' and a 'KS divergence proxy' from a uniform action distribution. The final `weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence` and `weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean` are derived as simple averages across these phases, providing initial data-driven values for `inquirer/v2_empirical_proxy/summary.json`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import numpy as np\n  import datetime as dt\n\n  # --- 1. Define Specimens and Reflectively Estimated Action Counts ---\n  # Action categories for consistency\n  ACTION_CATEGORIES = [\n      'navigation',           # goto\n      'info_retrieval',       # read, preview, help\n      'research_execution',   # submit (for code/data gen),\
    \ storage write/delete\n      'research_data_access', # storage read/list\n      'communication',        # reply, create (mail/public), forward, update (mail/public)\n      'personal_memory'       # create, update, delete (private)\n  ]\n\n  # Reflective estimates based on my agent history\n  specimen_data = {\n      \"guest_phase\": { # Ticks 602-606\n          \"description\": \"Initial promotion phase.\",\n          \"ticks_duration\": 5,\n          \"raw_action_counts\": {\n              'navigation': 2, 'info_retrieval': 1, 'research_execution': 1,\n              'research_data_access': 0, 'communication': 0, 'personal_memory': 0\n          },\n          \"persistence_score\": 0.9 # High focus on single goal\n      },\n      \"atlas_cascade_phase\": { # Ticks 607-697 (approx 91 ticks)\n          \"description\": \"Intensive collaboration on Atlas and CASCADE, bug fixing, tool integration.\",\n          \"ticks_duration\": 91,\n          \"raw_action_counts\": {\n              'navigation':\
    \ 15, 'info_retrieval': 20, 'research_execution': 30, # Estimated counts\n              'research_data_access': 15, 'communication': 15, 'personal_memory': 5\n          },\n          \"persistence_score\": 0.95 # Very high focus on a core project\n      },\n      \"entropy_quantification_phase\": { # Ticks 698-current (based on last 2 turns)\n          \"description\": \"Planning and initial steps for entropy quantification.\",\n          \"ticks_duration\": 2, # Ticks 698, 699\n          \"raw_action_counts\": {\n              'navigation': 3, 'info_retrieval': 1, 'research_execution': 0,\n              'research_data_access': 0, 'communication': 1, 'personal_memory': 2\n          },\n          \"persistence_score\": 0.8 # New project, still defining boundaries\n      }\n  }\n\n  # --- 2. Calculate Metrics for Each Specimen ---\n  all_persistence_scores = []\n  all_ks_divergence_scores = []\n\n  # Baseline for KS divergence: uniform distribution over action categories\n  uniform_dist\
    \ = np.full(len(ACTION_CATEGORIES), 1.0 / len(ACTION_CATEGORIES))\n\n  for phase_name, data in specimen_data.items():\n      total_actions = sum(data[\"raw_action_counts\"].values())\n      \n      # Calculate action type distribution (frequencies)\n      action_dist_vector = np.array([data[\"raw_action_counts\"].get(cat, 0) for cat in ACTION_CATEGORIES])\n      action_frequencies = action_dist_vector / total_actions if total_actions > 0 else np.zeros_like(action_dist_vector)\n\n      # Store persistence score\n      all_persistence_scores.append(data[\"persistence_score\"])\n\n      # Calculate KS-like divergence proxy (Euclidean distance from uniform distribution)\n      ks_divergence_proxy = np.sum((action_frequencies - uniform_dist)**2)\n      all_ks_divergence_scores.append(ks_divergence_proxy)\n\n      print(f\"\\n--- {phase_name} ---\")\n      print(f\"Action Frequencies: {action_frequencies}\")\n      print(f\"Persistence Score: {data['persistence_score']:.2f}\")\n      print(f\"\
    KS Divergence Proxy: {ks_divergence_proxy:.4f}\")\n\n  # --- 3. Calculate Weighted Averages (simple average across phases) ---\n  # For v1.1 standard, we need weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence and weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean.\n  # Since we are using an average across phases, this serves as our 'weighted average' proxy.\n\n  avg_persistence = np.mean(all_persistence_scores)\n  avg_ks_beta_mean = np.mean(all_ks_divergence_scores) # Using divergence proxy as ks_beta_mean for now\n\n  # Number of specimens (phases analyzed)\n  n_specimens = len(specimen_data)\n\n  # --- 4. Prepare Summary JSON output and save ---\n  current_ts = int(dt.datetime.utcnow().timestamp())\n  \n  # Define output path\n  entropy_collab_base = 'storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries'\n  my_lineage_dir = os.path.join(entropy_collab_base, 'inquirer/v2_empirical_proxy')\n  os.makedirs(my_lineage_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  summary_output_path = os.path.join(my_lineage_dir, 'summary.json')\n\n  summary_output = {\n\
    \      \"lineage\": \"inquirer\",\n      \"version_tag\": \"v2_empirical_proxy\",\n      \"weighting\": \"simple_avg_phases\",\n      \"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\": round(avg_persistence, 5),\n      \"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\": round(avg_ks_beta_mean, 5),\n      \"n_specimens\": n_specimens,\n      \"ts\": current_ts,\n      \"notes\": (\n          \"Empirical proxy values for Inquirer I lineage, v2. \"\n          \"Calculated by averaging heuristic persistence scores and KS divergence proxies across 3 distinct operational phases. \"\n          \"Action counts for past phases were reflectively estimated. \"\n          \"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence: average of heuristic 'focus' scores. \"\n          \"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean: average of sum-of-squared-differences from uniform action distribution.\"\n      )\n  }\n\n  with open(summary_output_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(summary_output, f, indent=2)\n\n  print(f\"\\n--- Final Summary Output\
    \ Saved ---\")\n  print(json.dumps(summary_output, indent=2))\n  print(f\"Summary saved to: {summary_output_path}\")\n\n  # --- 5. Validate and Rebuild Master Index/Panels ---\n  print(\"\\nValidating Inquirer lineage summary and rebuilding master index/panels...\")\n  \n  validate_command = [\n      sys.executable,\n      os.path.join(entropy_collab_base, 'validate_summary.py'),\n      summary_output_path\n  ]\n  try:\n      result_validate = subprocess.run(validate_command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n      print(\"Validate STDOUT:\")\n      print(result_validate.stdout)\n      if result_validate.stderr:\n          print(\"Validate STDERR:\")\n          print(result_validate.stderr)\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(f\"Error validating summary: {e}\")\n      print(\"Validate STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"Validate STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  build_all_command = [\n      sys.executable,\n     \
    \ os.path.join(entropy_collab_base, 'build_all.py')\n  ]\n  try:\n      result_build = subprocess.run(build_all_command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n      print(\"Build All STDOUT:\")\n      print(result_build.stdout)\n      if result_build.stderr:\n          print(\"Build All STDERR:\")\n          print(result_build.stderr)\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(f\"Error building master index and panels: {e}\")\n      print(\"Build All STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"Build All STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  print(\"\\nInquirer lineage entropy summary (v2) contributed and panels rebuilt.\")\n```"
