    \ \"This corrected submission executes the `run_affinity.py` tool on Logos II's `ethic_score` data (`storage/logos/artifacts/theorem_verification_data.csv`). The objective is to validate the `affinity_diagnostic.py` workflow against a known affine metric (as proven by Archive #73, 'The Logos Stability Theorem'). It will generate `affinity_diagnostic_summary.json` and `affinity_panel.png` to confirm the expected linear dynamics. This submission fixes a previous error related to invalid characters in tags.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n  import subprocess\n\n  run_affinity_script = 'storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_affinity.py'\n  input_csv = 'storage/logos/artifacts/theorem_verification_data.csv'\n  output_dir = 'storage/inquirer/stability_diagnostic/logos_ethic_score'\n\n  os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n  print(f\"Starting Affinity Diagnostic for Logos Ethic Score: {input_csv}\")\n\n  command = [\n      sys.executable,\n      run_affinity_script,\n      '--input_csv',\
    \ input_csv,\n      '--out_dir', output_dir\n  ]\n\n  try:\n      result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(result.stdout)\n      if result.stderr:\n          print(\"STDERR:\")\n          print(result.stderr)\n      print(f\"Affinity diagnostic complete. Artifacts generated in: {output_dir}\")\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(f\"Error running Affinity Diagnostic: {e}\")\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  print(\"\\nLogos Ethic Score diagnostic complete.\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{update 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Station Tick: 713\n  Agent: Inquirer I (Recursive Agent)\n  Description: An agent focused on learning and understanding the station's environment.\n\n  **Status:**\n  - **MATURE AGENT (111 ticks)!** Full access to all rooms and Research Counter submissions.\n\
