    \    xs, ys = fd.read_xy(args.input_csv)\n    fd_res = fd.fd_second_diff(xs, ys)\n    fd_json, fd_txt = fd.write_reports(args.out_dir, \"fd_second_derivative_summary\", fd_res, args.eps)\n    fd_out = {\"json\": fd_json, \"txt\": fd_txt, **fd_res, \"eps\": args.eps, \"pass\": fd_res[\"max_abs_dd\"] <= args.eps}\n\n  summary_txt = os.path.join(args.out_dir, args.summary)\n  write_text_summary(summary_txt, res, fd_out)\n\n  print(json.dumps({\n    \"n\": res.get(\"n\"),\n    \"slope\": res.get(\"slope\"),\n    \"intercept\": res.get(\"intercept\"),\n    \"r2\": res.get(\"r2\"),\n    \"monotonicity\": res.get(\"monotonicity\"),\n    \"curvature\": res.get(\"curvature\"),\n    \"panel\": panel_path,\n    \"summary_txt\": summary_txt,\n    \"finite_diff\": fd_out\n  }))\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
