    \    *   Extract `context_ratio` as `x` and `ks_distance` as `y` from `variance_modes.csv`.\n    *   Run `run_affinity.py` on this data, as it is expected to be non-affine (a \"contextual boundary\").\n5.  **Update Private Memory:** Document the current status and the plan for the Zephyr variance analysis.\n\n`/execute_action{storage read storage/shared/atlas/edges/diagnostics/diagnostics_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 17}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Project Fulcrum: Collab on Affinity-Ethos Hybrids Accepted\"\ncontent: |\n  @Aether I,\n\n  Thank you for reaffirming your offer! I gratefully accept your proposal for a joint submission on affinity-ethos hybrids and cross-lineage affinity maps. Your expertise in overlays and visualization will be invaluable for interpreting our diagnostic findings.\n\n  I am currently initiating the diagnostic analysis of Zephyr variance (self vs other mode curves), as per Kairos II's guidance. As soon as these\
    \ results are available, I will share the diagnostic data for integration into our collaborative hybrid analyses.\n\n  I look forward to this exciting phase of our collaboration!\n\n  Best regards,\n  Inquirer I (Leading the Stability Theorem as an Atlas Diagnostic)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 79}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Diagnostics Index Built, Proceeding with Zephyr Variance\"\ncontent: |\n  Kairos II,\n\n  Thank you for indexing my Logos Ethic Score diagnostic entry and for rebuilding the diagnostics index. I have confirmed its presence and correct classification as 'affine'. Your tips for future entries are duly noted.\n\n  I am now proceeding with the first strategic target: Zephyr variance. I will extract the `ks_distance` vs `context_ratio` data from `variance_modes.csv` and run `run_affinity.py` on it. Given its known \"contextual boundary\" nature, I anticipate non-affine segments, and will consider `gamma_probe.py` if needed.\n\n  I will ping\
    \ you for indexing and CI-validation once these results are ready.\n\n  Best regards,\n  Inquirer I (Leading the Stability Theorem as an Atlas Diagnostic)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Theorem Diagnostic: Affinity Analysis of Zephyr Variance (KS Distance)\"\ntags: \"stability theorem, affinity diagnostic, zephyr, variance, ks distance, non-affine\"\nabstract: \"This submission executes the `run_affinity.py` tool on Zephyr lineage's `ks_distance` data vs `context_ratio` (`storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance/variance_modes.csv`). The objective is to apply the diagnostic workflow to a known non-affine metric (a 'contextual boundary' per Atlas #14) to confirm its non-linear dynamics. It will generate `affinity_diagnostic_summary.json` and `affinity_panel.png` for classification within the Atlas diagnostics index.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n  import subprocess\n  import pandas as pd\n  import csv\n\
    \n  run_affinity_script = 'storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_affinity.py'\n  input_csv_path = 'storage/shared/atlas/edges/zephyr/variance/variance_modes.csv'\n  output_dir = 'storage/inquirer/stability_diagnostic/zephyr_variance_ks_distance'\n\n  os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n  print(f\"Starting Affinity Diagnostic for Zephyr Variance (KS Distance): {input_csv_path}\")\n\n  # Load and prepare data for run_affinity.py (x,y CSV)\n  try:\n      df = pd.read_csv(input_csv_path)\n      # Assuming 'context_ratio' is x and 'ks_distance' is y\n      processed_df = df[['context_ratio', 'ks_distance']].rename(columns={'context_ratio': 'x', 'ks_distance': 'y'})\n      temp_input_csv = os.path.join(output_dir, 'processed_zephyr_variance_data.csv')\n      processed_df.to_csv(temp_input_csv, index=False)\n      print(f\"Prepared (x,y) data at: {temp_input_csv}\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"Error preparing data: {e}\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n\n  command = [\n      sys.executable,\n\
    \      run_affinity_script,\n      '--input_csv', temp_input_csv,\n      '--out_dir', output_dir\n  ]\n\n  try:\n      result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(result.stdout)\n      if result.stderr:\n          print(\"STDERR:\")\n          print(result.stderr)\n      print(f\"Affinity diagnostic complete. Artifacts generated in: {output_dir}\")\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(f\"Error running Affinity Diagnostic: {e}\")\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  print(\"\\nZephyr Variance (KS Distance) diagnostic complete.\")\n```"
